# The built editor is a byte-exact artifact whose SHA-256 is recorded in
# public/app/manifest.json and verified in the browser before a single byte executes.
#
# Git's automatic line-ending conversion MUST NOT touch it. With core.autocrlf=true (the
# Windows default) a re-clone would rewrite every LF to CRLF, changing the bytes, breaking
# every digest, and the site would show "Refused to start" with no obvious cause. Marking
# these paths binary disables conversion in both directions, on every platform.
public/app/** -text -diff
public/app-locked/** -text -diff

# Everything else may be normalised to LF in the repository and checked out natively.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary types, listed so no future rule can catch them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.wasm binary
